users/AegisTTN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AegisTTN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AegisTTN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AegisTTN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AegisTTN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T13:55:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T11:34:07Z","body":"Basically this is not a specifically out of bounds bug, it happens for any action that causes the Tree to say its been moved/scrolled, or more in depth that cause `Tree::_scroll_moved` to run, which in the case of going out of bounds happens even if horizontal scrolling isn't visually happening (Such as adding a node with a small name, going out of bounds here will cause `Tree::_scroll_moved` to run even if nothing visually changed). So this happens, as side effect of #112998, on any dock that use a tree and when scrolling/going out of bounds and renaming.\n\nThis happens because `popup_editor`, in the case above this is a TextEdit that you use for the rename, gets hidden when a \"scroll\" is detected but this specific case doesn't tell the drag to stop, but as it's window has been hidden you become unable to stop it yourself unless you open it again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6193791623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]